cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the following metadata."
title: "Porphyrii: A Latin Poetry Scansion and Recitation Toolkit"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Zhiping"
    family-names: "Yang"
abstract: >-
  Porphyrii uses a two-stage online language model pipeline to identify Latin,
  restore lexical vowel quantities in context, translate the passage, and explain
  its grammar. A bounded deterministic solver scans dactylic hexameter, elegiac
  couplets, and isolated pentameters. Text-integrity checks compare the source
  letters with the restored text. A rule-based pronunciation engine follows
  W. S. Allen's Vox Latina and drives eSpeak NG WebAssembly formant synthesis
  in the browser. Saved passages support local history and offline recitation.
keywords:
  - "Latin poetry"
  - "scansion"
  - "prosody"
  - "text-to-speech"
  - "digital humanities"
  - "classical studies"
  - "Latin pedagogy"
license: AGPL-3.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-25
repository-code: "https://github.com/kalliyang/porphyrii"
url: "https://porphyrii.org"
